# The same history as histtools, but left PAUSED in the middle of a bisect.
#
# `bisect` is stateful across invocations and every case in the harness gets a
# pristine clone, so a multi-step bisect cannot be written as consecutive case
# lines. The paused state is therefore built here with real git -- `git bisect
# start main v1` marks c9 bad and c2 good and checks out the midpoint c5 --
# and each case probes exactly one step taken from that point.
#
# `bisect log` is captured to an untracked file so `bisect replay` has a real
# transcript to consume without a second command in the case line.
. "$(dirname "$FIXTURE")/histtools.fixture"
git bisect start main v1 > /dev/null 2>&1
git bisect log > bisect-transcript.txt 2>/dev/null
